Tech Mahindra” Interview Experience — GCP Cloud Ops Stack 🌩️

It was a great learning experience exploring the GCP Cloud Operations Stack in my recent interview with Tech Mahindra. The discussion covered both technical depth and situational awareness. Here’s a snapshot of the key areas touched during the conversation:

🔹 Core Questions:
•	What is your primary cloud?
•	Did you work in Terraform?
•	Can you write a Terraform program to create a user group and add yourself as an owner?
•	What are locals in Terraform? (With an example of using locals to create a compute instance)
•	How do you deploy applications on GCP?
•	Where do you deploy your apps in GCP?
•	What’s your primary automation scripting language?
•	Write a Linux shell script to clear logs older than 7 days.

🔹 Scenario / Behavioural Topics:
•	Describe your most challenging recent task.
•	Can you work in any shift for the Bengaluru location?
•	How much experience do you have in Cloud Ops?
•	Will you be able to start work after Knowledge Transfers (KTs)?
•	Would you be comfortable in an ODC setup where personal devices aren’t allowed?
